{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Mapping table: an Uberhand/4IFIR Wizard settings backup -> the CUST offsets of our field map. USED BY scripts/make-factory-defaults.mjs to turn the firmware's own Default.json into package/factory-defaults.json, which the generator then turns into service/Default.ini. It is also the groundwork for importing users' old backups - see docs/CONVERTER-CONCEPT.md; that import is deferred and NO menu section is generated from this file today.",
    "source_format": "atmosphere/kips/kip-json/*.json — an array of 54 entries, each with a parameter name, a hex value and the internal fields extent/filler_before/page. The entry order is stable, verified on Default.json and Eclipse.json.",
    "why_explicit": "The mapping is spelled out EXPLICITLY rather than matched by name. Automatic matching sends the voltage curve points to the wrong places: the point names of the Mariko and Erista curves are identical (\"307MHz\"), so a name match picks an arbitrary one. The converter writes into a live kip, and a miss here corrupts a table nobody will ever find afterwards.",
    "platform": "There is NO need to work out the revision from the file: the converter runs on the console, and the engine filters out the other revision's fields by the ;system= tag. Fields with platform mariko/erista are applied only on their own revision.",
    "length": "Where the backup has 4 bytes and the map has 3 — the top byte is always zero, the value is little-endian, and the first three bytes are taken. Verified against both reference files.",
    "verified_against": [
      "4ifir/atmosphere/kips/kip-json/Default.json",
      "4ifir/atmosphere/kips/kip-json/Eclipse.json"
    ]
  },
